1
00:00:00,167 --> 00:00:02,433
We all love Geet from Jab We Met.

2
00:00:02,433 --> 00:00:04,100
But I think we can agree,

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:05,400
girl desperately needed

4
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,400
a Life Design Lab lecture.

5
00:00:07,633 --> 00:00:10,533
She planned to run away and marry Anshuman,

6
00:00:10,533 --> 00:00:13,033
convinced she had her future figured out.

7
00:00:13,267 --> 00:00:14,267
Except...

8
00:00:14,267 --> 00:00:16,033
Anshuman was a hypothesis,

9
00:00:16,033 --> 00:00:17,233
not a plan.

10
00:00:17,967 --> 00:00:21,233
Life prototyping is about exploring a possible future

11
00:00:21,233 --> 00:00:22,933
through small experiments,

12
00:00:22,933 --> 00:00:24,800
so you can test assumptions

13
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,633
and learn before committing.

14
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:30,000
Geet could've started with a prototype conversation,

15
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,500
tried a low-stakes experience together,

16
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,467
and discovered if their plans actually matched.

17
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:38,033
Turns out, not every life decision

18
00:00:38,033 --> 00:00:40,600
needs a dramatic Bollywood plot twist.

19
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,333
Sometimes, it just needs a prototype.
